### Part 1: BBB230_merge.sh

# ===== STEP 1: Re-compress standard gzip files to bgzip =====#

Convert standard gzip (.vcf.gz) files into block-gzipped format so they can be indexed.

* command --> zcat | bgzip -c


# ===== STEP 2: Filter VCF files to standard chromosomes =====#

Remove unplaced scaffolds and random contigs (e.g., chr1000) that cause allele mismatch errors during merging. Retains only standard cattle chromosomes (1-29 and X).

* command --> bcftools view -r chr1,chr2,...,chr29,chrX



# ===== STEP 3: Index filtered input VCF files =====#

Create .csi indices for each filtered VCF file.

* command --> bcftools index --threads 4



# ===== STEP 4: Check for missing variants in the 3 VCF files =====#

* command --> bcftools isec -p vcf_diff_output \ BullsHDTom_filtered.vcf.gz \ BullsHD5_5_filtered.vcf.gz \ BullsHD_Extra8_filtered.vcf.gz

List the exact chromosome, position, and alleles (variants) that are missing from specific files and store them to vcf_diff_output\sites.txt

awk '$NF != "111" {print $NF}' vcf_diff_output/sites.txt | sort | uniq -c

# 110: Present in File 1 & File 2, missing in File 3
# 101: Present in File 1 & File 3, missing in File 2
# 011: Present in File 2 & File 3, missing in File 1
# 100, 010, 001: Unique to only one file



# ===== STEP 5: Merge VCF files =====#

Combine the 3 HD (High Density) .vcf files into a single unified dataset.

* command --> bcftools merge --threads 4 -O z -o HD_merged_output.vcf.gz


How does bcftools merge perform in case of missing variants in one file?:

- Inclusion: Any variant present in at least one input file is kept and written to the output merged VCF file.
- Missing Genotypes (./.): For the samples belonging to the files that do not contain that specific variant, bcftools merge inserts missing genotype data (./.) at that position.


# ===== STEP 6: Index merged output & extract sample IDs ===== #

Index the final merged VCF and extract unique sample IDs (NOANs).

* command --> bcftools index & bcftools query -l



$ sbatch BBB230_merge.sh>

-inputs:
    "HDTom20260121_5_VCF9_20260121.vcf.gz"
    "BullsHD_Extra8_5_VCF9_20230504.vcf.gz"
    "BullsHD5_5_VCF9_20230414.vcf.gz"


-outputs:
    "HD_merged_output.vcf.gz"
    "HD_merged_output.vcf.gz.csi"
    "unique_NOANs.txt"



