### Part 2: BBB825_HD_QC.sh

# ===== STEP 1: Convert Merged VCF to PLINK Binary Format =====#

Import the merged VCF file into PLINK 2 binary format (.bed/.bim/.fam) while setting the cattle chromosome count to 29.

* command --> plink2 --vcf HD_merged_output.vcf.gz --chr-set 29 --make-bed



# ===== STEP 2: Generate Bull Sex File ===== #

Create a sex file defining all samples as males (bulls, coded as `1`) to correctly handle the X chromosome without warnings.

The 0 test_id 1 format (generated by awk {print $1, $2, 1}) is required because of how PLINK internally tracks samples using a dual-identifier system:
 Family ID (FID) and Individual ID (IID).   

Here is why each component is structured that way:

The 0 (Family ID / FID): When you convert a VCF file into PLINK binary format (.bed/.bim/.fam), PLINK requires a Family ID for every sample. 

Because standard VCF files do not contain family groupings, PLINK defaults to assigning 0 (meaning "no family" or root family) to every sample's FID column.


The test_id (Individual ID / IID): This is the unique sample name or National Animal Number (NOAN) of the individual bull extracted directly from column 2 of the .fam file.

The 1 (The Sex Code): This is the value you are passing to PLINK to update. In PLINK, sex is numerically coded: 1 = male (bull), 2 = female, and 0 or NA = unknown.   

"Why PLINK needs this exact structure for --update-sex: " 
When you use the --update-sex command, PLINK cannot just look at a list of raw sample names. It expects a mapping file that matches its native database structure—meaning it needs to look up both the Family ID and the Individual ID together (0 + test_id) to ensure it applies the male code (1) to the exact correct animal.


* command --> awk '{print $1, $2, 1}' HD_merged_raw.fam > bull_sex.txt



# ===== STEP 3: PLINK Quality Control Filtering ===== #

Apply standard genomic QC thresholds for individual genotyping rate (`--mind`), marker call rate (--geno), minor allele frequency (--maf), and Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium (--hwe).

* command --> plink2 --bfile HD_merged_raw --update-sex bull_sex.txt --mind 0.10 --geno 0.05 --maf 0.01 --hwe 0.001 --make-bed



$ sbatch BBB825_HD_QC.sh -->

-inputs:
    "HD_merged_output.vcf.gz"


-outputs:
    "HD_merged_raw.bed", ".bim", ".fam" (Raw merged binary files)
    "bull_sex.txt" (Sample sex mapping file)
    "HD_filtered_qc1.bed", ".bim", ".fam" (Final QC-filtered dataset)







